Expected elements: present

Identity bar (exit to `aztec`, hash, `Partial`, block, eight stepping buttons, scrubber, `128 / 1315`, phase rail), Code pane positioned at line 32, Call Trace/Event Log as one tab region with Call Trace open, Values pane below it with ten rows, Transaction pane whose first labelled row is `Data` with a toned badge and the producer's own sentences. No provenance band above the bar, no prose band, no spinner, no empty pane, Values is not a tab.

A genuinely dense tool surface, but the ~190 px the removed band returned was not spent on information: it went into leading and into a paragraph.

The `Data` row is now the least dense element on the page — eight lines of right-aligned, ragged-left prose across a ~35-character measure, ~230 px (≈23%) of the Transaction pane, and it pushes the chain fields down far enough that `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` is clipped at the viewport edge. Meanwhile the middle column is 46% empty: 332 px blank below `By call order.` and 129 px below `i`. Code sits at ~23 px pitch on ~13 px mono (≈1.75) — nine more lines would fit at desktop-app leading.

Fixes: set the `Data` sentences left-aligned and full-width in the pane; let the tab region size to its frames so the column's slack is not stranded.

Rating: 7/10

